---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../../styles/product.css';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Product" description="Dimension-driven parametric modeling, assemblies, simulation, CAM, PLM, reverse engineering, and a team of AI agents in one document. In the browser, or on Windows, Linux, and macOS.">
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Product</p>
      <h1>One environment, from constrained sketch to posted G-code.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Chudware is dimension-driven parametric CAD on exact solid geometry — a fillet is a real surface, not a triangle mesh pretending to be one. Modeling, assemblies, simulation, CAM, PLM, and a team of AI agents all work on the same document and the same feature tree. Reverse engineering brings scans, photos, and datasheets into that document with the evidence still attached.</p>
      <ul class="product-hero-meta">
        <li>Exact solids, not mesh approximations</li>
        <li>Dimension-driven models in native <code>.step+</code> files</li>
        <li>Browser workspace, or desktop app for Windows, Linux, and macOS</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="capabilities-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow" id="capabilities-title">Capabilities</p>
        <h2>Eight workspaces. One model.</h2>
        <p class="lede">Model it, assemble it, analyze it, machine it, and track it &mdash; without leaving the project.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="product-hub-grid">
        <article class="product-card product-card-lead">
          <p class="product-card-index">01 / Model</p>
          <h2><a href="/product/modeling/">Parametric modeling</a></h2>
          <p>Dimension-driven models. Fully defined 2D sketches drive ordered features, and the Feature Manager keeps every step human-editable instead of collapsing it into dead geometry.</p>
          <ul class="fact-list">
            <li>Named relations and driving dimensions, with degrees-of-freedom reporting</li>
            <li>Extrude, Revolve, Loft, Sweep, Pattern, Fillet, Shell</li>
            <li>Native <code>.step+</code> keeps tree, dimensions, materials, studies, and drawings</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="product-card">
          <p class="product-card-index">02 / Assemble</p>
          <h2><a href="/product/assemblies/">Assemblies</a></h2>
          <p>Components are located by mates against a fixed base, not by typed coordinates.</p>
          <ul class="fact-list">
            <li>Concentric, coincident, distance, and angle mates</li>
            <li>Interference checks and clearance inspection before release</li>
            <li>Stable component identity keeps mates and BOM rows connected</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="product-card">
          <p class="product-card-index">03 / Simulate</p>
          <h2><a href="/product/simulation/">Simulation</a></h2>
          <p>Studies stay attached to the design. Every result reports its mesh, reactions, convergence, and solver provenance so you can actually review it.</p>
          <ul class="fact-list">
            <li>Static, adaptive, convergence, modal, fatigue, thermal, buckling, and contact workflows</li>
            <li>Per-body materials plus bonded, contact, and free interface policies</li>
            <li>Mesh-quality, equilibrium, plausibility, and provenance fields beside the engineering result</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="product-card">
          <p class="product-card-index">04 / Mesh + solve</p>
          <h2><a href="/product/polymesh/">PolyMesh FEA</a></h2>
          <p>The public PolyMesh project combines CAD-aware volume meshing, a linear-elastostatics solver, recovery-based error estimation, and adaptive refinement.</p>
          <ul class="fact-list">
            <li>Public C++20 source and validation evidence under BSD 3-Clause</li>
            <li>Standard finite elements and polyhedral VEM in one global assembly</li>
            <li>Pinned commit recorded in Chudware simulation provenance</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="product-card">
          <p class="product-card-index">05 / Manufacture</p>
          <h2><a href="/product/cam/">CAM</a></h2>
          <p>Jobs are built from the active part, so the manufacturing plan stays attached to the design that produced it.</p>
          <ul class="fact-list">
            <li>Stock, work coordinate system, tool library, and process-ordered operations</li>
            <li>Toolpath simulation with tool, holder, stock, and rapid moves visible</li>
            <li>Posted G-code targeted at a specific machine and controller profile</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="product-card">
          <p class="product-card-index">06 / Collaborate</p>
          <h2><a href="/product/plm/">PLM</a></h2>
          <p>A project is the boundary for designs, assemblies, manufacturing artifacts, and revision history.</p>
          <ul class="fact-list">
            <li>Revisions with notes instead of <code>bracket_final_v7</code> filenames</li>
            <li>Specifications, photos, reports, and supplier files tracked as project items</li>
            <li>Handoff carries the deliverable and the decision trail together</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="product-card">
          <p class="product-card-index">07 / AI</p>
          <h2><a href="/product/copilot/">AI copilot</a></h2>
          <p>Describe the outcome. A team of agents splits the job across the workspace, drives the same modeling tools you use by hand, and leaves behind a human-editable feature tree.</p>
          <ul class="fact-list">
            <li>Inspect geometry, build and edit features, run studies, prepare CAM, measure and render</li>
            <li>Bring your own AI provider account or API key</li>
            <li>Anything that touches a physical machine waits for you</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="product-card">
          <p class="product-card-index">08 / Reverse engineer</p>
          <h2><a href="/product/reverse-engineering/">Reverse engineering</a></h2>
          <p>A session keeps the source, the scale, the reconstruction, and the review together, so a scan or photo never turns into an unexplained shape.</p>
          <ul class="fact-list">
            <li>Photos, video, webcam, scan meshes, datasheets, and library records as starting points</li>
            <li>Human-confirmed scale and fit dimensions, with single-photo shapes tagged approximate</li>
            <li>Deviation review, provenance history, Parts attachment, and full-session export</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="scope-title">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <header class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow" id="scope-title">Commercial preview</p>
        <h2>Try it on the work you actually need to ship.</h2>
        <p class="lede">Modeling, assemblies, simulation, CAM, PLM, reverse engineering, and the copilot are all available today. Chudware is in commercial preview: advanced workflows are still changing, so test it on a project that looks like yours before moving production work.</p>
        <p class="supporting-copy">Desktop builds for Windows, Linux, and macOS are on the download page. Desktop and Studio plans are on the pricing page.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="product-note">
        <p class="eyebrow">Reviewable output</p>
        <p>Every feature the agents build is in the tree with its sketch fully defined. Study evidence, CAM setup, and revisions stay visible too. You inspect what was produced; you never have to trust a summary sentence.</p>
        <p><a class="text-link" href="/pricing/">Compare plans <Icon name="arrow-right" /></a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="elsewhere-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow" id="elsewhere-title">Go deeper</p>
        <h2>Screenshots, docs, and pricing.</h2>
      </header>
      <ul class="product-crosslinks">
        <li class="product-crosslink">
          <h3><a href="/gallery/">Gallery</a></h3>
          <p>Modeling, CAM, and simulation examples with their requests and results.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="product-crosslink">
          <h3><a href="/docs/">Documentation</a></h3>
          <p>Guides for sketching, your first part, assemblies, CAM, PLM, reverse engineering, the copilot, installation, and keyboard shortcuts.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="product-crosslink">
          <h3><a href="/pricing/">Pricing</a></h3>
          <p>Trial, Desktop, Studio, education rates, storage, and enterprise.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section cta-band">
    <div class="wrap section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Start anywhere</p>
      <h2>Open the workspace, or read how a part gets built first.</h2>
      <p class="lede">Start the trial, or follow the first-part guide before you decide.</p>
      <div class="actions"><a class="button" href="https://app.chudware.com/signup">Create an account</a><a class="button button-secondary" href="/docs/first-part/">Build your first part</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
